From 79bebf20e2244b46b470184fed2ce5e05193f90f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:05:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden client viewer access (step 1)

- A project code alone no longer opens a project: it must be entered on the
  project's share link. The home page and legacy /project/<code> URLs now
  return the same instruction for every code and never reveal a share link
  (the legacy route previously redirected a valid code to its link, with no
  rate limit on GET).
- Per-link lockout: after 10 wrong codes in an hour, from any number of IP
  addresses, the link refuses all codes until the window passes. The existing
  per-IP limit stays in place.
- Viewer sessions expire after 12 hours; pages and file downloads then ask
  for the code again. File downloads also require the session's link token.
- Security headers on every response: nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY,
  Referrer-Policy strict-origin-when-cross-origin (Google Maps still receives
  the app origin for its referrer restriction), Permissions-Policy, and HSTS
  when secure cookies are on. Viewer pages add noindex and no-store.
- Tests: new tests/test_viewer_security.py (8 tests); existing tests updated
  for link+code entry. Per-module results match main (same two pre-existing
  failures in test_launch_diagnostics and the rate-limit pruning test).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
